(FUN-44 — LANGUAGE.md:885. "Writing an argument right after the
 function name with none of these words is an error naming the missing
 preposition, not a call with that argument dropped." Hand-verified: the
 diagnostic names the dropped-in token and the four accepted
 prepositions, and is anchored at the token itself, not at the call.
 Also hand-verified with a bare (unquoted) single-word function name
 (`announce count.` -> the same shape of diagnostic, token `count`) —
 the rule is not specific to quoted multi-word names.
